      "utf8": "from the official disclosures, most house reps and \nsenators largely have buy and hold portfolios with  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 536000,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the occasional trade here and there that wouldn't \nreally be considered outside the ordinary for most  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 540480,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "relatively wealthy career professionals. Now, \nthat might sound like I'm devil's advocating  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 544960,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a bit here, but it's actually the opposite. \nIt instead shows that the outperformance in  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 549440,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "congressional stock trades are largely driven by a \nsmall group of extremely active traders. In fact,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 554800,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "most of these elected officials actually did \nworse than the market as a whole. According  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 559200,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to the data that has been disclosed from 2025, \njust under a third of congressional portfolios  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 564000,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "outperformed the S\u0026P 500, but that was the same \nyear where Congress as a whole was up over 20%  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 569200,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "above the already strong returns of the broad \nmarket. In plain English, what this means is that  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 573920,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there are a few dozen elected officials who are \nmaking absolute bank and pulling up the average  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 578400,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "considerably. Congress as a whole on average is \nnow making over 10,000 trades a year, largely  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 583920,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "concentrated amongst just a handful of people. The \nmedian number of trades made by a congressperson  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 588960,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "was just three, raising the question of how these \nother people have time to do anything else. Now,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 594320,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I know this goes against the narrative that all \nof them are in on it, but that's actually a good  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 598960,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "thing. It shows that people who are clearly gaming \nthe system are a minority and that we can actually  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 604160,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "hold these officials to a higher standard. But \nbefore you get too optimistic, remember this  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 608960,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is still a how money works video. So the second \nthing we found when we compiled this data is who  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 614160,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "those Congress members making all of this money \nactually were. The reality is that it was largely  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 618960,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "more senior Congress people who were sitting on \nlots of committees. And almost every year since  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 623120,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "these disclosures were introduced, the party that \nhas controlled the House outperformed the party  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 627360,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that was in the minority on their stock trades. \nThese special committees give them access to even  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 631760,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "more information than they would get as regular \nlawmakers, letting people like Nancy Pelosi trade  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 636400,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in Nvidia while shaping the chips act or Tommy \nTuberville dabbling corn futures while serving  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 641040,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on the Agricultural Committee. Now, mercifully, \nmuch smarter people than me at the National Bureau  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 645760,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of Economic Research actually found the same trend \nto corroborate these findings. The study revealed  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 650480,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that lawmakers generally perform similar to their \npeers until they are put into a leadership role,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 655280,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at which point they outperform their peers by 47 \npercentage points on average, which in the world  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 660000,
    "dDurationMs": 6880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of investing is an unfathomably large gap. In \n2025, these insiders again considerably outperform  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 666880,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the market and their peers in Congress. The only \npeople from this group to actually lose money were  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 671360,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Chip Roy, who got absolutely hammered on a single \nenergy stock and has since become a major advocate  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 676480,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of limiting congressional stock trading, and Mitch \nMcConnell, who reported a net trading loss of 1.8%  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 682160,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the year. And that is probably the closest I \nwill ever get to defending Mitch McConnell. Oh,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 686800,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "yeah. And the third thing we found out when \npouring through this data is that even though  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 690320,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it is technically publicly available, they have \nmade it about as difficult as humanly possible  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 694720,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to find. The user interface that you need to use \nin order to find disclosures looks like it was  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 699120,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "straight out of the 1990s and the information is \npresented very unintuitively. Throw on some low  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 704240,
    "dDurationMs": 6560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "poly gifs and you can almost hear the dialup tone. \nAgain, for a law passed in 2012. Now, thankfully,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 710800,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if you don't feel like subjecting yourself to \nthis, you can also find a lot of this information  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 714800,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on third party websites that track this data \nas well. So, I will leave a link to that below.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 719840,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Unfortunately, the reason that there are so many \nthird party tools that track this data so closely  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 724560,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is because, well, people just try to make money \nby copying the trades of their elected officials,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 730160,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which is not great, but at least it gives us some \nuser-friendly transparency. Finally, of course,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 735600,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the Stock Act only applied to members of Congress \nand their staff. It doesn't include the president,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 740560,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "cabinet members, or other highranking officials, \nand it certainly doesn't include the off-the-book  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 745120,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "transactions like the one that inspired this \nvideo in the first place. But even still,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 749280,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from what we know, how much is all of this \nactually costing us? Well, collectively, from what  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 754240,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "has been legally disclosed, Congress specifically \nonly does about a billion dollars worth of trading  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 759120,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "volume in a single year, which is clearly an \ninsane amount of money for a totally random  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 763680,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "representative cross-section of our country. But \nit's also not enough to meaningfully move markets  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 768400,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by itself. The real cost, of course, is how these \nfinancial incentives alter their decision-making.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 773760,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Is someone on the agricultural committee going to \npropose policy that helps farmers but hurts their  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 778160,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "corn futures? Will someone who owns millions \nof dollars worth of Nvidia bail out the AI  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 782480,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "industry? And is it worth undermining trust in our \ngeopolitical channels to make a few million on oil  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 788240,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "futures? These decisions impact how much we pay in \ninterest, the validity of our trade deals, and the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 793600,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "strength of our currency. Our economic uncertainty \nindex is now higher than it has been at any point  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 798960,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "outside of the pandemic, which just on our debt \nalone means we need to offer higher interest rates  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 804000,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to offset the increased risk that now comes with \nlending to America. This has more than doubled  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 808960,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "our interest repayments over the past 5 years \nalone. Something that we are all eventually going  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 813440,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to pay through higher taxes, higher inflation, or \njust good old-fashioned economic default. Again,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 819280,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this is also just one avenue where this political \nself-s serving is coming back to bite us. Is  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 824400,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "insider trading exclusively responsible for our \ndebt risk premium? Of course not. But it does  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 829440,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "mean that there are direct financial incentives \nnot to fix it. But if you want to know how much  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 833680,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "worse this particular problem can get, go watch \nthis video next to find out why we haven't had a  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 838320,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "debt crisis yet. And don't forget to like and \nsubscribe to keep on learning how money works."
    } ]
  } ]
}
